# PipiUI AI workspace rule

[`CONSTITUTION.md`](../../CONSTITUTION.md) is binding and is the single
source of truth.

- Supported external tool slugs are `codex|claude|cursor|kimi|qoder|zcode`;
  each uses `ai/<tool>/*`. Kimi CLI, Qoder, and ZCode use the binding root
  `AGENTS.md` without duplicated tool-specific rules or copied local
  permissions. PipiUI Boss is the only native-lifecycle exception.
- Create Cursor tasks from current green with
  `./scripts/new-ai-worktree.sh --tool cursor ... --base integration/green`.
- Open and edit only the returned linked worktree.
- Run `./scripts/verify-worker.sh` for a real debug compile + relevant tests.
- Do not package a release App by default; use `--package-preview` only when a
  local runnable preview is explicitly needed.
- Do not merge green into an active divergent task. Retire completed worktrees
  and create the next task from current green.
- Staging has exactly one lifecycle owner. Never integrate/promote during an
  active Boss wave, and never start/resume Boss while external
  integration/promote owns staging. The shell lock does not coordinate with
  native `MainRepoSerialQueue`.
- Promote a Boss candidate only after terminal state, no active/recovery agent,
  passed post-merge verify, and clean staging.
- Never install or replace `/Applications/PipiUI.app`; only the integration
  owner may integrate, promote green, merge green to main, and ship.
- Do not merge, clean another workspace, or claim canonical delivery.
